title: Pro Power Onboard with Vehicle Off
raw_community_title: Enable Pro Power Onboard with truck off (2022-2023 only. Standard
  on 2024+)
category: Powertrain and Drivetrain
platform: F-150 Lightning
model_years: 2022-2023
trim: All
validated: true
verified_by: Kyle / AsBuiltPro & Lightning Community
source_sheet: F-150 Lightning FORScan Thread
notes: Creates a Sync toggle in the Pro Power settings screen. Requires a 2025 or
  later PCM update (via FDRS) or early 2026 Charge Port OTAs (PT-25.13.12 or PT-25.8.5
  depending on model year).
steps:
- module: APIM
  address: 7D0-10-03
  mask: xxxx xx*x xx--
  nibbles:
  - nibble: 6
    recommended_hex: '2'
    community_instruction: Set to 2
    bits:
    - bit: 3
      action: 0
      feature_name: Extended Play Time Override (EPTO)
      target_state: Disabled
    - bit: 2
      action: 0
      feature_name: Digital Owner's Manual  (DOM)
      target_state: Disabled
    - bit: 1
      action: 1
      feature_name: Digital Owner's Manual  (DOM)
      target_state: Enabled
    - bit: 0
      action: 0
      feature_name: Digital Owner's Manual  (DOM)
      target_state: Disabled
- module: APIM
  address: 7D0-10-04
  mask: xxx* xxxx xx--
  nibbles:
  - nibble: 3
    community_instruction: If 0, change to 8. If 4, change to C. If 6, change to E.
      If you enabled the Advanced Charging Screen, you likely have a 6.
    bits:
    - bit: 3
      action: 0
      feature_name: PPO Utility Idle (PPOUI)
      target_state: Disabled
    - bit: 2
      action: 0
      feature_name: Record Feedback (RF)
      target_state: Disabled
    - bit: 1
      action: 0
      feature_name: Record Feedback (RF)
      target_state: Disabled
    - bit: 0
      action: 1
      feature_name: Record Feedback (RF)
      target_state: Enabled
validation_status: validated
